      <div class="member-summary-grid">

        <section class="member-summary-box">
          <h2>Research Area</h2>
          <p>
            Adaptive scheduling and resource allocation in IEEE 802.15.4
            TSCH and 6TiSCH-based IoT networks, with emphasis on scalable,
            energy-efficient and reliable communication under dynamic,
            bursty and mobility-affected traffic conditions.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="member-summary-box">
          <h2>Supervisors</h2>
          <p>
            Prof. Nikumani Choudhury, BITS Pilani Hyderabad Campus, and
            Prof. Wei Xiang, La Trobe University.
          </p>
        </section>

      </div>

      <div class="member-detail-layout">

        <nav class="member-detail-nav" aria-label="Profile sections">
          <a href="#education">Education</a>
          <a href="#research">Research Focus</a>
          <a href="#publications">Publications</a>
          <a href="#milestones">Academic Milestones</a>
          <a href="#experience">Experience</a>
          <a href="#contact">Contact</a>
        </nav>

        <div class="member-detail-sections">

          <section class="member-detail-section" id="education">
            <h2>Education</h2>
            <ol>
              <li>
                <strong>Doctor of Philosophy, 2024–Present</strong><br>
                Joint doctoral researcher at BITS Pilani, Hyderabad Campus,
                and La Trobe University, Melbourne.
              </li>
              <li>
                <strong>Master of Technology in Electronics and Communication Engineering, 2016–2018</strong><br>
                North-Eastern Hill University, Shillong.
              </li>
              <li>
                <strong>Bachelor of Technology in Electronics and Communication Engineering, 2011–2015</strong><br>
                Lovely Professional University, Punjab.
              </li>
            </ol>
          </section>

          <section class="member-detail-section" id="research">
            <h2>Research Interests and Technical Focus</h2>
            <ul>
              <li>6TiSCH-based IoT network scheduling</li>
              <li>Adaptive slotframe design and resource allocation</li>
              <li>Low-power wireless networks using IEEE 802.15.4 TSCH</li>
              <li>Traffic-aware and event-driven scheduling</li>
              <li>Latency, reliability and energy optimisation</li>
              <li>Mobility-aware scheduling in multi-hop IoT networks</li>
              <li>Smart-city and industrial IoT communication systems</li>
            </ul>
          </section>

          <section class="member-detail-section" id="publications">
            <h2>Selected Publications</h2>
            <ol>
              <li>
                <strong>FlexiFrame: Adaptive Slotframe Scheduling for 6TiSCH-Based Smart City IoT Networks</strong><br>
                Accepted at IEEE GLOBECOM Workshops 2025.
              </li>
              <li>
                <strong>TARA: Topology-Aware Rank Allocation for Load Balancing in Autonomous Scheduling of 6TiSCH-based IoT Networks</strong><br>
                Accepted at IEEE ANTS 2025.
              </li>
              <li>
                <strong>ASCP: Analytical Slotframe Control Policy for Adaptive Resource Allocation in 6TiSCH Networks</strong><br>
                Accepted at IEEE ICC 2026.
              </li>
            </ol>
          </section>

          <section class="member-detail-section" id="milestones">
            <h2>Academic Milestones</h2>
            <ol>
              <li><strong>August–December 2024:</strong> PhD coursework.</li>
              <li><strong>January 2025:</strong> PhD qualifying examination.</li>
              <li><strong>April 2025:</strong> PhD proposal seminar.</li>
              <li><strong>Expected January–December 2027:</strong> Research visit at La Trobe University.</li>
            </ol>
          </section>

          <section class="member-detail-section" id="experience">
            <h2>Research and Teaching Experience</h2>
            <p>
              Joint doctoral researcher through the Asian Smart Cities
              Research and Innovation Network, with research activity spanning
              BITS Pilani, Hyderabad Campus, and La Trobe University.
            </p>
            <ul>
              <li>Computer Architecture — Teaching Assistant</li>
              <li>Computer Networks — Teaching Assistant</li>
              <li>Operating Systems — Teaching Assistant</li>
              <li>Object Oriented Programming — Teaching Assistant</li>
            </ul>
          </section>

